course: dictionary
lesson: 4088
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, so you must read the words around them to find the right one. Ask what fits the whole sentence. «Alice felt giddy after the Cat vanished, so she had to sit down.» Feeling dizzy fits best here, because she needed to sit down.
explain: The same word can describe a feeling. «The class was giddy with excitement on the last day of term.» Giddy does not mean dizzy here. It means so happy and excited that you cannot keep calm, and the word «excitement» is your clue.
explain: Giddy can also describe a height that makes you dizzy, as in «a giddy height», or a person who is silly and not serious, as in «a giddy girl». Check the clues before you decide, and try your meaning in the sentence to see if it still makes sense.
fact: Giddy is an adjective, and it changes to giddier and giddiest.
fact: «Giddy» means dizzy: feeling that everything is spinning and you might fall.
fact: «Giddy» can also mean so excited that you cannot keep calm, as in «giddy with excitement».
fact: If you feel giddy, sit down so you do not fall, and tell an adult if it keeps happening, because it can mean you need water, food or a doctor.
exercise: «The roundabout spun faster and faster, and Mia felt giddy.» What does giddy mean here? | Happy and calm | *Dizzy, as if everything is spinning | Very tall | Silly and rude
exercise: «The class was giddy with excitement before the trip.» What does giddy mean? | Dangerously high | Dizzy after spinning | Old and slow | *So excited that it was hard to keep calm
exercise: In «a giddy height», what does giddy mean? | Very cheap | Tiny and quiet | Very cold and icy | *Making you feel dizzy when you look down
test: Alice says, «You make one quite giddy.» What is the Cat doing to her? | Making her laugh | *Making her feel dizzy | Making her hungry | Making her sleepy
test: «The silly girl giggled and twirled, giddy and carefree.» What does giddy suggest? | *Silly and not serious | Very old | Sad and tired | Dizzy after being spun
exam: In «Alice felt giddy and sat down», what should you do if you feel giddy yourself? | Keep running fast | *Sit down so you do not fall | Stand on a chair | Spin round again
